---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Tokens
description: The three token tiers, and every token with its value in each mode.
---

{#
  What the tiers are, and the full reference. How a token is named is on its
  own page, Tokens Nomenclature (foundations/nomenclature.njk).
#}

<dl class="stat-row">
  <div class="stat">
    <dt>Tokens</dt>
    <dd>{{ tokens.stats.total }}</dd>
  </div>
  {% for tier in tokens.tiers %}
    <div class="stat">
      <dt>{{ tier.tier | capitalize }}</dt>
      <dd>{{ tier.count }}</dd>
    </div>
  {% endfor %}
  <div class="stat">
    <dt>Vary by mode</dt>
    <dd>{{ tokens.stats.modeVarying }}</dd>
  </div>
</dl>

<h2>Overview</h2>

<p>
  Every visual decision in QDS lives in one place and travels one path. A raw value
  becomes a <strong>primitive</strong>, a primitive is given meaning as a
  <strong>semantic</strong> token, and a semantic token is applied by a
  <strong>component</strong> token. Nothing skips a tier, and nothing points
  backwards.
</p>

<p>
  That structure survives into the CSS rather than being flattened at build time,
  which is what makes a single stylesheet themeable:
</p>

<pre><code>--qds-component-button-primary-color-background-rest: var(--qds-semantic-color-background-primary-rest);
--qds-semantic-color-background-primary-rest:         var(--qds-color-blue-600);
--qds-color-blue-600:                                 #2563eb;</code></pre>

<p>
  Switching to dark mode redefines the middle line and nothing else: only
  {{ tokens.stats.modeVarying }} of {{ tokens.stats.total }} variables are
  redeclared to do it. Reach for a <strong>semantic</strong> token in product
  code, since it switches with the theme; override a <strong>component</strong>
  token to restyle a component.
</p>

<p>
  Every token's name follows one grammar, checked at build time. The
  <a href="/foundations/nomenclature/">Tokens Nomenclature</a> page sets it out: each
  tier's anatomy, the allowed vocabularies, and how the build enforces them.
</p>

<h2>Token reference</h2>

<p>
  The primitive and semantic tiers. Values are read from the generated token
  manifest, so they are the values the CSS actually ships. <strong>Resolves through</strong> walks each token down to
  the raw value it ends at.
</p>

<div class="token-filter">
  <qds-input
    id="token-filter"
    type="search"
    label="Filter tokens"
    placeholder="Filter by name or value, such as background or #2563eb"
  ></qds-input>
  <p id="token-filter-status" class="token-filter__status" role="status"></p>
</div>

<qds-tabs id="token-tiers" label="Token tiers">
  {% for tier in tokens.tiers %}{% if tier.tier != 'component' %}
    <qds-tab slot="tab" data-tier="{{ tier.tier }}">{{ tier.tier | capitalize }} <span class="tab-count">{{ tier.count }}</span></qds-tab>
  {% endif %}{% endfor %}
  {% for tier in tokens.tiers %}{% if tier.tier != 'component' %}
    <qds-tab-panel data-tier="{{ tier.tier }}">
      <p class="tier-intro">
        {% if tier.tier == 'primitive' %}
          Raw values. No references, and no tier identifier in the variable name.
        {% else %}
          Intent, aliasing primitives. The only tier where light and dark differ.
        {% endif %}
      </p>
  {% for group in tier.categories %}
    <h3 id="{{ tier.tier }}-{{ group.category }}" class="token-category">{{ group.category }}</h3>

    {% set rows = group.tokens %}
    {% include "partials/token-table.njk" %}
  {% endfor %}
    </qds-tab-panel>
  {% endif %}{% endfor %}
</qds-tabs>

<h2>Component tokens</h2>

<p>
  Each component's tokens are its public styling API: overriding one is the
  supported way to restyle that component. They are listed with the component
  they belong to, on its <strong>Tokens</strong> tab, where they make sense.
</p>

<ul class="token-components">
  {% for family in docs.families %}{% if family.tokenCount %}
    <li>
      <a href="{{ family.tokensUrl }}" data-token-sets="{{ family.tokenSets | join(' ') }}">{{ family.name }}</a>
      <span class="token-components__count">{{ family.tokenCount }}</span>
    </li>
  {% endif %}{% endfor %}
</ul>

<script type="module" src="/assets/token-reference.js"></script>
